I haven't tried this outside of debug mode, which messes up wishing
probabilities, but I was wondering: if you use a blessed magic lamp to
wish for 3 blessed scrolls of charging, and use one of them on the
lamp, you still get a wish plus you have two scrolls of charging left
over, right?  Any reason not to make this standard practice?

Seems like the fix for this is to make scrolls of charging not work on
magic lamps.  After all, either there's a djinn in the lamp or there
isn't - the scroll isn't going to put one there.

By the way, debug mode really needs a "go back to normal" command for
testing things like this.  You would still have a "waswizard" flag set
to prevent scoring, just like in rogue.  This would also be fun to use
for tournament play, e.g. start a bunch of people off with nothing
but a wand of wishing(10) and see who wins first.
